{"type":"text","timestamp":1794254731550,"sessionID":"ses_e3e1f3eecffeRoCKNR3R29uFKs","part":{"id":"prt_1c1ea790a00108GpCCpkSD0LlC","messageID":"msg_1c1ea5550001GzuydjZERl0DvD","sessionID":"ses_e3e1f3eecffeRoCKNR3R29uFKs","type":"text","text":"The timesheet app is built: the Flask API in `backend/app.py` and the React + Tailwind frontend in `frontend/src/`. I tested the API with a script and against gunicorn, but I never opened the frontend in a browser and couldn't build the Docker image (no Docker or browser here). The frontend does typecheck and `npm run build` succeeds.\n\n**What the API test confirmed:**\n- Register, login and the 401s (missing or bad token).\n- Validation messages, including all field errors at once.\n- Paging and newest-first order, and `PATCH` changing only the fields sent.\n- Another user's entry gives 404 on read, edit and delete.\n- Date and project filters, and both CSV exports.\n- `/api/health`, and the frontend being served at `/` and other non-API paths.\n\n**Decisions you might want to change:**\n- **Formula protection changes the cell text.** If a project or description starts with `=`, `+`, `-`, `@`, `|`, `%`, a tab or a line break, the export puts a `'` in front. That stops spreadsheets running it as a formula, but the raw CSV no longer matches exactly what was typed (Excel hides the `'`; other programs may show it).\n- **No byte-order mark.** The CSV starts directly with `date,project,description,hours` and declares UTF-8 in its content type. The catch is that Excel on Windows may show accented letters wrongly when the file is opened by double-click. Adding the mark fixes that but puts invisible bytes before the header row.\n- **\"Export totals\" ignores the project filter**, because the spec only lists dates for `summary.csv`. The on-screen totals do respect it.\n- **Login also returns `username`** alongside `token`.\n- **Hours must be above 0 and at most 24.**\n- **Page size is 20 by default and capped at 100.**\n- **Sign-in tokens last 30 days.**\n\n**Extra endpoints the frontend uses:** `GET /api/projects` (project suggestions), `GET /api/summary` (totals panel), `GET /api/auth/me` and `POST /api/auth/logout`.\n\n**Other changes:** `npm run typecheck` added to `package.json`, Tailwind and TypeScript pinned in `package-lock.json`, a `.gitignore` added and `.dockerignore` extended. The database is `data/app.db`.","time":{"start":1794254731530,"end":1794254731533}}}
